    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Using the current local stress state stored on the model in the variable &quot;stress&quot;, this <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_interrelation" kindref="compound">Interrelation</ref> subclass computes the failure criterion &apos;failure&apos; performing a Mohr Coulomb analysis, but without consideration of the fluid pressure.</para>
<para>To apply this interrelation the following discretised variables need to be defined:</para>
<para>&quot;stress&quot;, &quot;mean stress&quot;, &quot;cohesion&quot;, &quot;failure&quot;. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
